window.MNM_QUICK.route["6-10"]="<div class=\"sc-wrap\"><p class=\"sc-pick\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> No start city picked: choose one in the <b>Start</b> box in the top bar to see its route for levels 6–10.</p><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"ailvorith\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Ail&#x27;Vorith · levels 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 6–10: Fungal armor, House quest Part 1, Blind Midden top floor</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor monk\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor, Monk only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Start your class House quest with your Obsidian Shackle (Obsidian Academy or Military Outpost). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-xal\"><summary><b>House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl Part 1: 8+, Part 2: 13+</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest: chest armor at 8, city access, House Xal&#x27;tharn faction and the Iron Render weapon.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Klavel Sul</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Foreign Quarter, Military Outpost: the building on the left past the bridge and gate, back of the room with the melee trainers (the quest page calls it the Obsidian Academy; see the Monk trainer note)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Part 1: 8+, Part 2: 13+</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Inquisitor, Monk</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>Obsidian Shackle from the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest. Deep Common language.</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Part 1 grants city access (wiki). Part 2 turn-in: &#x27;You gain faction with House Xal&#x27;tharn&#x27;. Other faction hits are marked as unknown on the wiki: no sourced data yet.</td></tr></table><h5>Steps <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h5><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Part 1 (8+): hail Klavel Sul; say &#x27;The Queen&#x27;, then &#x27;I would be a cenobite&#x27;, then &#x27;Do you have a task for me?&#x27;. You receive the Remnant Satchel (6 slots).</li><li>Swim around the west of the city, where elementals and skulls patrol the west island shores. Kill a separated skull and a spectral remnant (both 8-11) for 6 Lost Skull.</li><li>Combine the satchel and hand it to Klavel Sul (XP). Say &#x27;I swear allegiance to the Queen!&#x27; (XP). Inquisitors receive the Dull Iron Cuirass; Monks the Simple Chestwrap.</li><li>Part 2 (13+): before 13, Klavel says you lack the skill. At 13, hail him and say &#x27;I accept.&#x27; He gives a summons for Lady Miniel in the Shol&#x27;tar, beneath the Queen&#x27;s arena: take the road on the right into the Dark City and go through the dungeon gates near the bank.</li><li>Give the summons to Miniel Ubast in the Inquisitor&#x27;s Guildhall (NPC page: enter the main city, turn right, up the ramp, the prison guarded by Inquisitors, up one floor and through the door). Ask about the duty and where the exiles are.</li><li>Go to the exile camps to the south, by the river into the Great Cavern Sea: past the waterfall where snakes gather, on the bottom floor past the invisible hired thug. Kill exiles until you have one each of the Unknown, Silver and Gold Sigil of a Lesser House (unique: one of each).</li><li>Keep killing the bottom-floor exiles until Gullach Otal&#x27;qar (16-17, named Fighter) spawns in their place, then kill him for Gullach&#x27;s Head.</li><li>Hand the 3 sigils and the head to Miniel Ubast.</li></ol><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Lost Skull x6</b>: a separated skull (8-11, Enchanter: Mesmerize, Silence), a spectral remnant (8-11, Fighter), west island shores</li><li><b>Sigil of a Lesser House (Unknown, Silver, Gold)</b>: exiles: a starving outcast, a runaway, a praying exile (exile mobs are 15-22)</li><li><b>Gullach&#x27;s Head</b>: Gullach Otal&#x27;qar (16-17), bottom floor of the exile area behind the hired thug</li></ul><p><b>Turn in:</b> Part 1: Klavel Sul. Part 2: Miniel Ubast (Shol&#x27;tar, inside the city)</p><p><b>Rewards:</b> XP: XP at both Part 1 turn-ins and at the Part 2 turn-in · Item: Inquisitor: Dull Iron Cuirass (chest AC 9, STA +1, INT +1, HP +5) and Iron Render (1H slash 7/30, STR +2, STA +1, INT +1, HP +5, Mana +5). Monk: Simple Chestwrap and Tarnished Iron Bo. · Coin: none listed · Faction: City access (Part 1); House Xal&#x27;tharn + (Part 2)</p><p><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Reward conflict resolved, Cuirass wins. The quest page listed a Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant from its first version (2026-09-23, beta 0.30.0.0) until rev 78132 (2026-10-07, after the 0.30.2.1 release patch), when an editor replaced it with the Dull Iron Cuirass for Inquisitors. That editor created the Dull Iron Cuirass item page with full stats four minutes later. The Pendant item page was last touched 2026-09-26, and the Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests summary page that still says Pendant was never updated. The newer first-hand edit with an item page wins over the older summary. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)&amp;action=history\">Wiki edit history: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Dull_Iron_Cuirass\">Wiki: Dull Iron Cuirass (item page created 2026-10-07)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Xal%27tharn_Pendant\">Wiki: Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant (item page, last edited 2026-09-26)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span></p><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> Whether Monks (or pre-release characters) still get the Pendant as well: no sourced data yet. No talk page exists for the quest. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Xal%27tharn_Pendant\">Wiki: Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant (item page, last edited 2026-09-26)</a></span></p><p><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Do Part 2 at about 15-17, not 13: the sigil exiles are 15-22 and Gullach is 16-17 (wiki levels). Bring a group or a healer. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-xaltharn-quest\">quest helper</a> · <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Klavel_Sul\">Wiki: Klavel Sul (rev 82871, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Miniel_Ubast\">Wiki: Miniel Ubast</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Sigil_of_a_Lesser_House_(Gold)\">Wiki: Sigil of a Lesser House (Gold)</a></span></p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric paladin\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric, Paladin only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-drez\"><summary><b>House Drezzorith (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 8+</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (city access, the Lexicon of Mysteries line for Clerics).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Zalethra Drezzorith</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>8+</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Cleric, Paladin</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>House of Drezzorith (+); Citizens of Ail&#x27;vorith (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive Small Burlap Pouch from Zalethra Drezzorith.; You receive Lexicon of Mysteries from Zalethra Drezzorith.; You receive Letter for Alarys from Zalethra Drezzorith.; You receive Empty Sample Box from Alarys Drezzorith.; You receive Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries from Alarys Drezzorith.; You receive Advanced Lexicon of Mysteries from Tal Drezzorith.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>House Acceptance</b></li><li>Zalethra Drezzorith is located in the Obsidian Academy upper floor. From the bridge and gate into the Foreign Quarter, enter the building straight ahead with caster trainers and go upstairs.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Small Burlap Pouch from Zalethra Drezzorith.</li><li>Cross the bridge and turn right at the Toilmaster. Follow the water&#x27;s edge until your reach a cave full of cultists. Kill an angry cultist, an agitated cultist, a cultist priestess to collect 7 Cultist Eye to fill the bag.</li><li>Combine the container into Filled Burlap Pouch and return it to Zalethra Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Lexicon of Mysteries from Zalethra Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Letter for Alarys from Zalethra Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: House of Drezzorith (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Ail&#x27;vorith (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Faction with House of Drezzorith increased to High Indifferent</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Faction with Citizens of Ail&#x27;vorith increased to High Amicably</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Goblin Samples</b></li><li>Alarys Drezzorith is located in a building in the main city of Ail&#x27;Vorith, 4th floor, south side... just southeast of the high level Paladin and Cleric trainers. You can see it on the left side standing on the main bridge leading into the city.</li><li>Hand Alarys Drezzorith your Letter to Alarys.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Empty Sample Box from Alarys Drezzorith.</li><li>Kill a Deepgulp warrior, a Deepgulp scavenger, a Deepgulp hunter, a Deepgulp berserker to collect 6 Sample of Mind Control Substance and combine them to create Full Sample Box.</li><li>(Alternately, you can complete the Thanetal&#x27;s Samples quest handing in 1 Deep Ale and 10 silver to acquire 6 Sample of Mind Control Substance.)</li><li>Hand Full Sample Box to Alarys Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Any faction hits? EXP?</li><li>Hand Lexicon of Mysteries to Alarys Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries from Alarys Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Any faction hits? EXP?</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Continuation - Part 2</b></li><li>Tal Drezzorith is located in the building next to Alarys Drezzorith, directly across from the cleric/paladin guild</li><li>Hand the Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries in to Tal Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Advanced Lexicon of Mysteries from Tal Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Any follow-up breadcrumbs?</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Drezzorith_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-drezzorith-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-11</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter rogue\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter, Rogue only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-ith\"><summary><b>House Ith&#x27;vayen (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (belt reward, city access).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Enchanter, Rogue</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive a Letter to Aleyz.; You receive a Cloth Belt of Runes.; You receive a Leather Belt of Runes.; You receive a Roasted and Poisoned Fish.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - A Letter of Recommendation - Req. Lvl 1</b></li><li>Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen is located in the front left corner of the first floor of the caster hall in the Obsidian Academy.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: You do not have to use the teleport to complete the quest.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: You are teleported out of the city and to the left across the bridge, up the ramp and to the right (most of the way to the zone safe point).</li><li>Upon turning in eight Myconid Parts:</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive a Letter to Aleyz.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive a Cloth Belt of Runes.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive a Leather Belt of Runes.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 2 - A Letter of Recommendation - Req. Lvl 1</b></li><li>Begins when you turn in a Letter to Aleyz to Aleyz Ith&#x27;vayen inside the main city.</li><li>Bring one Fire Elemental Stone, three Sample of Tainted Water and one Whitefish to Aleyz.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive a Roasted and Poisoned Fish.</li><li>Return to Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen. Stealth behind her and use the MUD commands /look table.</li><li>While holding the Roasted and Poisoned Fish use the MUD command /place table.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: As of 2026-10-12, this MUD command appears to be bugged and is not triggering correctly.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: More information is required...</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Ith%27vayen_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-ithvayen-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-12</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade wizard\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade, Wizard only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-hal\"><summary><b>House Hal&#x27;kareth (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (Hal&#x27;kareth Signet Ring).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Myal Vehear</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Spellblade, Wizard</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - ?</b></li><li>Myal Vehear is located in the Obsidian Academy, 2nd floor.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>a note for vhaleth hal&#x27;kareth</b></li><li class=\"dim\">Note: More information is required...</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Hal%27kareth_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-halkareth-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-10</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer ranger\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Archer, Ranger only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-vael\"><summary><b>House Vael&#x27;xirith (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Laren Drin&#x27;dar</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Archer, Ranger</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive Scalp Pouch from Laren Drin&#x27;dar.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - Goblin Scalps</b></li><li>Laren is located in the Military Outpost with the melee class instructors. From the bridge and gate into the Foreign Quarter, enter the building across, second on the left (not the bank tunnel). He is on the right, near back of the room.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Scalp Pouch from Laren Drin&#x27;dar.</li><li>Go kill a bunch of goblins and return.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Faction hits? Follow-up? Reward? Related NPCs?</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Vael%27xirith_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-vaelxirith-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-13</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist necromancer\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist, Necromancer only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-varros\"><summary><b>House Varros (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (House Varros faction).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Vaslir Naiyth</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Elementalist, Necromancer</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>House Varros (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); House Varros;</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1</b></li><li>Vaslir Naiyth is located in the Obsidian Academy. As you enter the academy, she is located near the stairs in the back of the room on the right.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: House Varros (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: House Varros (+)</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 2</b></li><li>Vaslir Vharkith is located near the top of Ail&#x27;Vorith proper, next to some other Vaslir NPCs.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Find the Escaped Slave</b></li><li>Although Laeran Birchshade cons as &quot;Ready to attack&quot;, he does not attack on sight. He may either be killed for Vharkith&#x27;s Research Notes or spoken with instead. Speaking with him also begins a separate optional quest involving the Birchshade Family Bracelet. See Laeran Birchshade for details.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Speak with Vaslir Maryn</b></li><li>Vaslir Maryn is located near Vaslir Vharkith in the upper area of Ail&#x27;Vorith, standing beside the large fountain. Vaslir Kiannes is also located nearby.</li><li>At this point there are two confirmed routes for obtaining Flask of Essairyl. You may gather elemental essences for Vaslir Maryn, or speak with Vaslir Kiannes and complete his water-sample task instead. You only need to complete one route.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Gather the Elemental Essences =</b></li><li>4 Essence of Elemental Air</li><li>4 Essence of Elemental Earth</li><li>Only the Air and Earth elementals are needed for this step. Water elementals can also be found around the shores near Ail&#x27;Vorith proper, but they do not provide the essences Maryn requests.</li><li>There are also Water elementals along the shoreline surrounding the city. Make sure you are hunting Air Elementals and Earth Elementals for this quest.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Return to Vaslir Maryn =</b></li><li>4 Essence of Elemental Air</li><li>4 Essence of Elemental Earth</li><li>the Corpse Dust given to you by Vaslir Vharkith</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Route B: Earn Essairyl from Vaslir Kiannes</b></li><li>Vaslir Kiannes is located near Vaslir Maryn and Vaslir Vharkith in the upper area of Ail&#x27;Vorith, near the fountain.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Gather the Water Samples =</b></li><li>10 Sample of Tainted Water</li><li>Corpse Dust</li><li>This is an alternative to gathering Essence of Elemental Air and Essence of Elemental Earth for Vaslir Maryn. You do not need to complete both routes.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: House Varros (+)</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Obtain Nerolir</b></li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Purchase Nerolir from Miral =</b></li><li>The exact item name and item details for Nerolir still need to be verified from the in-game item window.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Return Nerolir to Vaslir Vharkith =</b></li><li>The exact hand-in dialogue, experience reward, faction change, and any other reward from the Nerolir turn-in still need to be confirmed.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>The Note and the Order</b></li><li>It still needs to be confirmed whether receiving the Letter to Freysia Riftrend also awards experience or House Varros faction.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Retrieve Vharkith&#x27;s Order =</b></li><li>Vharkith&#x27;s Order</li><li>Belot&#x27;s exact location, level, NPC class, spawn conditions, and complete loot table still need to be documented. It should also be confirmed whether Vharkith&#x27;s Order is a guaranteed drop.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Return Vharkith&#x27;s Order =</b></li><li>The dialogue, experience reward, faction change, item rewards, and continuation of the quest after returning Vharkith&#x27;s Order still need to be documented.</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Varros_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-varros-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-10</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-velg\"><summary><b>House Velgarrith (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (Frayed Cloak of House Velgarrith).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Xilonen Velgarrith</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Shadow Knight</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - Req. Lvl 2</b></li><li>Xilonen Velgarrith is located upstairs in the martial trainer building</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: More information is required...</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Velgarrith_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-velgarrith-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-13</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> From level 5: farm cave myconids (5-7) for the Fungal Armor Quests. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Armor_Quests\">Wiki: Fungal Armor Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-fungal\"><summary><b>Fungal Armor Quests</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 5</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Four armor pieces for 14 classes, including Inquisitor, plus Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith faction toward banking and vendors.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Leatherworker Vex</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Foreign Trader&#x27;s Market, Foreign Quarter</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>5</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>Deep Common language. The class list on the items is ARC BRD BST CLR DRU FTR INQ MNK PAL RNG ROG SHD SHM SPB (no pure casters).</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Each piece: House Velgarrith + and Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith + (wiki).</td></tr></table><h5>Steps <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h5><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Hail Leatherworker Vex, then ask &#x27;What is something that could keep me alive longer?&#x27; and say &#x27;I seek protection.&#x27;</li><li>Ask &#x27;What Coat?&#x27;, &#x27;What Helm?&#x27;, &#x27;What Leggings?&#x27; or &#x27;What Boots?&#x27; for each piece&#x27;s recipe.</li><li>Coat: 3 Perfect Fungus Cap, 2 Strong Fungus Hyphea, 1 Perfect Fungus Stem. Helm: 2 Cap, 1 Hyphea. Leggings: 2 Stem, 2 Hyphea, 2 Perfect Fungus Volva. Boots: 2 Volva, 2 Hyphea.</li><li>Hand each set of parts to Vex to receive that piece (XP and faction each).</li></ol><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Full set: 7 Strong Fungus Hyphea, 5 Perfect Fungus Cap, 4 Perfect Fungus Volva, 3 Perfect Fungus Stem</b>: a cave myconid (5-7)</li></ul><p><b>Turn in:</b> Leatherworker Vex</p><p><b>Rewards:</b> XP: Experience per piece · Item: Fungal Coat (AC 7), Fungal Helm (AC 5), Fungal Leggings (AC 6), Fungal Boots (AC 4) · Coin: none listed · Faction: House Velgarrith +, Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith +</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Armor_Quests\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-fungal-armor-quests\">quest helper</a> · <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Armor_Quests\">Wiki: Fungal Armor Quests</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Coat\">Wiki: Fungal Coat (class list)</a></span></p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Camps (wiki levels): a cave myconid 5-7, a bubbling oozeling 5-7, a Deepgulp runt and a Deepgulp explorer 6-7 (their kills raise Ail&#x27;vorith Exiles), a skeleton 6-7, a cave snake 7-9, cultists 6-7 (cave along the water&#x27;s edge, right of the Toilmaster). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27vorith_Exiles\">Wiki faction: Ail&#x27;vorith Exiles</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Drezzorith_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Drezzorith (Quest)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor monk\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor, Monk only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> At 8+: the west island shores (swim around the west of the city) have a separated skull and a spectral remnant (8-11) for Xal&#x27;tharn Part 1, plus elementals and spirits (9-11). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Blind Midden top floor: 6-7 prisoners and outcasts, and named mobs at level 7 (Gorgeous, Flavic the Fisher, Mucky Morgurah, Forager Davra, Sethrine the Unblinking) with gear drops. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Blind_Midden\">Wiki: Blind Midden (rev 83212)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-merit\"><summary><b>Mark of Merit</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1 (repeatable)</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> XP and Marks of Merit for the Midden Mark Menu while you clear Blind Midden named mobs.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Blind Midden ground floor (map point 1)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1 (repeatable)</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>None listed.</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><h5>Steps <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h5><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Kill any named mob in Blind Midden and loot its corpse item (no drop).</li><li>Turn the corpse in to Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra.</li></ol><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Corpse of &lt;named&gt;</b>: any Blind Midden named (top floor named are 7-12, basement named 15+)</li></ul><p><b>Turn in:</b> Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra</p><p><b>Rewards:</b> XP: Experience · Item: Blind Midden Mark of Merit (Midden Mark Menu rewards are random) · Coin: none listed · Faction: no sourced data yet</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mark_of_Merit\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-mark-of-merit\">quest helper</a> · <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mark_of_Merit\">Wiki: Mark of Merit</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Blind_Midden\">Wiki: Blind Midden (rev 83212)</a></span></p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor only</span> <span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Order: fungal pieces while you level on myconids (5-8), then Xal&#x27;tharn Part 1 at 8-9 for the Dull Iron Cuirass and city access. Visit Nurvol Cereveth every time you reach a spell level. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Armor_Quests\">Wiki: Fungal Armor Quests</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Lurithos Kest): L6 Net Shot; L7 Flare, Snaring Shot; L8 Interrupting Shot, Strafing Barrage I; L9 Piercing Shot I; L10 Alarm Trap, Point Blank II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Chant of Purity; L7 Repel; L8 Lento&#x27;s Aria of Stillness, Vellicosa&#x27;s Fanfare; L9 Languid Lullaby; L10 Dissonant Vocalization. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Pounce; L7 Chop I; L8 Remedy Companion, Savage Spirit; L9 Command: Kill; L10 Enraging Strike II, Maul I. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Zalethra Drezzorith): L8 Dispel Magic, Fear the Dead, Heal, Invisibility versus Undead, Lesser Redemption, Poison Protection, Promise of Mending I, Rebuke III, Resilience, Sense Magic, Shackle, Summon Food. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Cure Disease, Mantle of Summer, Mantle of Winter, Prickly Barrier, Sense Magic, Speed of the Wild, Summer&#x27;s Warmth, Summon Drink, Summon Food, Swarm of Mites, Twisting Roots, Winter&#x27;s Chill. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Lothur Varros): L8 Companion Strike II, Dispel Magic, Flame Shield, Minor Creation: Fire, Summon Arrows, Summon Minor Manastone, Summon Minor Water Trident, Summon Throwing Dagger. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen): L8 Enchant Tin Bar, Illusion: Ogre, Lesser Enlightenment, Lesser Group Enlightenment, Lesser Vespyra&#x27;s Veil, Magic Protection, Minor Strength, Root, Runeskin, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Tharkan Inathar): L6 Armor Break; L7 Distracting Taunt; L8 Clobber, Intimidation; L9 Challenging Arrow I; L10 Rend II, Shield Bash I. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Nurvol Cereveth): L6 Silence, Ward of Suspicion; L7 Fire Protection; L8 Censuring Strike II, Dominate the Mind, Pillage Mana, Sense Magic; L9 Dispel Magic; L10 Purifying Blow, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Klavel Sul): L6 Sneak; L7 Pinning Throw; L9 Stone Stance; L10 Round Kick II. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vaslir Naiyth): L8 Aspect of Vampirism, Blood Pact, Dispel Magic, Eye of the Underworld, Feign Death (Spell), Holy Protection, Invisibility, Lesser Unliving Shield, Life Drain II, Pact of Deathly Enduring, Poisonous Deluge, Rot Flesh, Summon Minor Lifestone, Terrify the Dead. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Mentvar Drezzorith): L6 Invisibility versus Undead; L7 Shield Toss; L8 Crusader Strike II, Fear the Dead, Healing Touch, Lay on Hands; L9 Blind; L10 Cure Poison, Restorative Smite. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Laren Drin&#x27;dar): L6 Swift Shot; L7 Invisibility versus Beasts; L8 Minor Mantle of the Hunter, Shroud, Taunt; L9 Barbed Shot, Twisting Roots; L10 Hunter&#x27;s Focus, Rending Cut, Survivor Stance. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Zorvanna Velgarrith): L6 Slice I; L7 Uppercut; L8 Sap; L9 Poison Tolerance; L10 Stab II. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vhalrek Velgarrith): L6 Grip of Shadow; L7 Cold Protection, Holy Protection; L8 Grip of Agony, Shadow Strike II, Siphoning Slash, Soul Servant, Soulrend II; L10 Aura of the Unholy, Lord of Shadows, Pulling Shadows, Reave, Terror in the Shadows. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Ancestor&#x27;s Eye, Ghostly Blight, Greater Malady, Invisibility versus Undead, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Pact of Haste, Pact of Renewal, Purge, Speed of the Wild, Spirit Bane III, Spirit Mending, Summon Food. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Ilnara Hal&#x27;kareth): L6 Magic Protection; L7 Phase Strike; L8 Conduit, Dispel Magic; L9 Electricity Protection; L10 Discharge, Electric Infusion, Infused Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vhasilla Hal&#x27;kareth): L8 Blink, Dispel Magic, Glyph: Mun, Insidious Magic, Lesser Spellshield, Minor Arcane Surge, Minor Iceblast, Sorcerous Mind, Spell Catalyst, Summon Mage Light. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"faelindral\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Faelindral · levels 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 6–10: Fellstone orcs, wolf den, widows</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Fellstone orcs: warriors and necromancers 5-7, Fellstone shamans 7+, guards 8+, trackers 8-10, ragecallers 9+, defilers 10+. Named: Scout Leader Krindor (6, on the ridge past the Kennel Lift bridges) and Vorkuul Blighteye (7). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Beastmaster_Starter_Quest_(Faelindral)\">Wiki: Beastmaster Starter Quest (Faelindral) (rev 82724, 2026-10-17)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Wolves, west along the hillside path near the Druid Ring (solo 9, group 6-10; a good leather source): beguiled wolves ~7-8, a beguiled alpha wolf (8-10, named), and Rotmuzzle (9) with rabid wolves and skeletons. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Spiders: elder widows and widow matrons 7-8; Mezzatrian Boneweaver (7-9, a Necromancer spider). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Named: Kyros Emeraldscale (8, across the river west of the Newbie Lift bridge; drops the Poison Duct for the drakeling coat and pants). Fossergrim watchers 9-11, Meluli Dawnglow 8-12?. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Keeper&#x27;s Bight edge (by Evershade Weald): bight asps ~8-9, forest whelps 10-11, black bears 10-12. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Keeper%27s_Bight\">Wiki: Keeper&#x27;s Bight</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-faelindral-sixeyes\"><summary><b>Six Eyes Too Many</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Pixie Glitter (used in the Bard starter) for 6 Widow Eyes. Court of Summer + and Court of Winter −.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Polietta Two-tone</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Evershade Weald · Polietta Two-tone, up on the hill near the fae guardians (daytime only)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Court of Summer (+); Court of Winter (-)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>Pixie Glitter; (exp);</td></tr></table><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Widow Eye x6</b>: black widows (4-5) and elder widows (7-8)</li></ul><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Locate Polietta Two-tone, who spawns in Evershade Weald during the day up on the hill near the Fae Guardians.</li><li>Hunt a black widow and an elder widow until you have collected 6 x Widow Eye.</li><li>Hand 6 x Widow Eye to Polietta Two-tone.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Court of Summer (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Court of Winter (-)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Pixie Glitter from Polietta Two-tone.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Pixie Glitter is used for Bard Starter Quest (Faelindral).</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Six_Eyes_Too_Many\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-six-eyes-too-many\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-09-27</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional (long, travels to Night Harbor): <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-faelindral-sweet\"><summary><b>A Sweet Treat</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> A long chain from Faelindral to Night Harbor: Defenders, Citizens and Smallfolk Alliance faction, 55 silver in total, and the Stein of Baker&#x27;s Scorn. Starts with one Jelly Cupcake for Guard Pippi Pinecone.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Guard Pippi Pinecone</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Evershade Weald</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Defenders of Faelindral (+); Citizens of Faelindral (+); Smallfolk Alliance (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>Stein of Baker&#x27;s Scorn, 1; Half of a Jelly Cupcake, 1; (exp); (money: 55S)</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Note: Guard Pippi Pinecone has ambient dialogue that clues the observant player on how to initiate this quest.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>The Hungry Guard</b></li><li>Give Guard Pippi Pinecone 1 x Jelly Cupcake, which you can obtain from completing Mierra&#x27;s Famed Cupcakes.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Defenders of Faelindral (+)</li><li>Head to Mierra Willowshade near the inn.</li><li>Bring 12 x Royal Jelly and 1 x Satchel to Mierra Willowshade.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Faelindral (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Packaged Cupcakes from Mierra Willowshade.</li><li>Deliver 1 x Packaged Cupcakes to Guard Pippi Pinecone.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Packaged Cupcakes from Guard Pippi Pinecone.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Delivery</b></li><li>Travel to the Smallfolk District, south of Saltbreeze Park, in Night Harbor and search for Guard Halfsies. You can ask other guards in the area about Pete Pinecone as well.</li><li>Hand the Packaged Cupcakes to Guard Halfsies.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Smallfolk Alliance (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive {{Money 0 0 5 0</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Half of a Jelly Cupcake from Guard Halfsies.</li><li>Travel to Chef Violyn, who is located at the Crimson Oasis Inn near the North Gate of Night Harbor.</li><li>Hand the Half of a Jelly Cupcake to Chef Violyn.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Violyn&#x27;s Grocery Basket from Chef Violyn.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Violyn&#x27;s Grocery List from Chef Violyn.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>A Fiery Treat</b></li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Additional information regarding collection of the grocery list items would be beneficial.</li><li>Violyn&#x27;s Grocery List notes the required items, but not where to obtain them. Chef Violyn is not willing to help, either.</li><li>Purchase 2 x Dried Dragon&#x27;s Breath Pepper from Spices Merchant in Night Harbor.</li><li>Purchase 1 x Baladi from the Mukhtar Brewery in the river pirate tavern.</li><li>Purchase 4 x Basilisk Seasoning from An exotic cook in Shallow Shoals.</li><li>Purchase 2 x Viper&#x27;s Kick which can be obtained from the Viper&#x27;s Kick Recipe quest.</li><li>Combine 2 x Dried Dragon&#x27;s Breath Pepper, 1 x Baladi, 4 x Basilisk Seasoning, and 2 x Viper&#x27;s Kick in Violyn&#x27;s Grocery Basket.</li><li>Turn in Violyn&#x27;s Full Grocery Basket to Chef Violyn in Night Harbor.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Smallfolk Alliance (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Some of the following dialogue is incomplete and needs correction.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Violyn&#x27;s Special Batch of Cupcakes from Chef Violyn.</li><li>Give Violyn&#x27;s Special Batch of Cupcakes to Guard Halfsies.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Smallfolk Alliance (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Half of Violyn&#x27;s Cupcake from Guard Halfsies.</li><li>Give Half of Violyn&#x27;s Cupcake to Chef Violyn.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Smallfolk Alliance (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive {{Money 0 0 50 0</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Stein of Baker&#x27;s Scorn from Chef Violyn.</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest as needing more information. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_Sweet_Treat\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-a-sweet-treat\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-06</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Keyaryn Thornshade): L6 Net Shot; L7 Flare, Snaring Shot; L8 Interrupting Shot, Strafing Barrage I; L9 Piercing Shot I; L10 Alarm Trap, Point Blank II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Pine Brightreed (starter); Sylphrena Starfall and Laenyth Windharp): L6 Chant of Purity; L7 Repel; L8 Lento&#x27;s Aria of Stillness, Vellicosa&#x27;s Fanfare; L9 Languid Lullaby; L10 Dissonant Vocalization. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Relgen Greenblade, then Aerin Mossfang): L6 Pounce; L7 Chop I; L8 Remedy Companion, Savage Spirit; L9 Command: Kill; L10 Enraging Strike II, Maul I. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Dispel Magic, Fear the Dead, Heal, Invisibility versus Undead, Lesser Redemption, Poison Protection, Promise of Mending I, Rebuke III, Resilience, Sense Magic, Shackle, Summon Food. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (High Gatekeeper Sylvarya Starveil): L8 Cure Disease, Mantle of Summer, Mantle of Winter, Prickly Barrier, Sense Magic, Speed of the Wild, Summer&#x27;s Warmth, Summon Drink, Summon Food, Swarm of Mites, Twisting Roots, Winter&#x27;s Chill. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Companion Strike II, Dispel Magic, Flame Shield, Minor Creation: Fire, Summon Arrows, Summon Minor Manastone, Summon Minor Water Trident, Summon Throwing Dagger. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Enchant Tin Bar, Illusion: Ogre, Lesser Enlightenment, Lesser Group Enlightenment, Lesser Vespyra&#x27;s Veil, Magic Protection, Minor Strength, Root, Runeskin, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Vaelric Ironbark, then Craftguard Vinebrow): L6 Armor Break; L7 Distracting Taunt; L8 Clobber, Intimidation; L9 Challenging Arrow I; L10 Rend II, Shield Bash I. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Silence, Ward of Suspicion; L7 Fire Protection; L8 Censuring Strike II, Dominate the Mind, Pillage Mana, Sense Magic; L9 Dispel Magic; L10 Purifying Blow, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Sneak; L7 Pinning Throw; L9 Stone Stance; L10 Round Kick II. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Aspect of Vampirism, Blood Pact, Dispel Magic, Eye of the Underworld, Feign Death (Spell), Holy Protection, Invisibility, Lesser Unliving Shield, Life Drain II, Pact of Deathly Enduring, Poisonous Deluge, Rot Flesh, Summon Minor Lifestone, Terrify the Dead. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Invisibility versus Undead; L7 Shield Toss; L8 Crusader Strike II, Fear the Dead, Healing Touch, Lay on Hands; L9 Blind; L10 Cure Poison, Restorative Smite. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Relgen Greenblade): L6 Swift Shot; L7 Invisibility versus Beasts; L8 Minor Mantle of the Hunter, Shroud, Taunt; L9 Barbed Shot, Twisting Roots; L10 Hunter&#x27;s Focus, Rending Cut, Survivor Stance. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Elyndiir Nightshade): L6 Slice I; L7 Uppercut; L8 Sap; L9 Poison Tolerance; L10 Stab II. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Grip of Shadow; L7 Cold Protection, Holy Protection; L8 Grip of Agony, Shadow Strike II, Siphoning Slash, Soul Servant, Soulrend II; L10 Aura of the Unholy, Lord of Shadows, Pulling Shadows, Reave, Terror in the Shadows. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Varilis Thornvine): L8 Ancestor&#x27;s Eye, Ghostly Blight, Greater Malady, Invisibility versus Undead, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Pact of Haste, Pact of Renewal, Purge, Speed of the Wild, Spirit Bane III, Spirit Mending, Summon Food. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Magic Protection; L7 Phase Strike; L8 Conduit, Dispel Magic; L9 Electricity Protection; L10 Discharge, Electric Infusion, Infused Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Blink, Dispel Magic, Glyph: Mun, Insidious Magic, Lesser Spellshield, Minor Arcane Surge, Minor Iceblast, Sorcerous Mind, Spell Catalyst, Summon Mage Light. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"night-harbor\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Night Harbor · levels 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 6–10: Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane, Shaded Dunes Ashira, smuggler beach</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane (wiki 3-15), next to Night Harbor: skeletal fighters 3-10, warriors 4-11, cavaliers 6-10. Named Timmon Bell and Jakob Geffrey (~8), Lieutenant Gregan Snyde and Ariblast the Wicked (10). Hunting guide: solo 8, group 4-14, good gear drops. Player-tracked: most at 13. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Tomb_of_the_Last_Wyrmsbane\">Wiki: Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.wiki/zones/tomb-of-the-last-wyrmsbane\">monstersandmemories.wiki: Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane (player-tracked levels and coin)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Several class quests run through the Tomb: the Paladin starter (Engraved Coin upstairs), Wizard (4) and Necromancer and Shaman (8) steps. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Tomb_of_the_Last_Wyrmsbane\">Wiki: Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Shaded Dunes: the Ashira camps near the Tel Ekir zone line (group 6-10), with the zone line handy if pulls go wrong. Dhajr Spitemaw (8+) is at the large Ashira camp and raises Red Mantles. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Shaded_Dunes\">Wiki: Shaded Dunes</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Red_Mantles\">Wiki faction: Red Mantles</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Shaded Dunes smugglers and wererats beach party, the furthest camp west along the south coast (6-9), with Toma the Two-Faced (9+). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monme.no/camps\">monme.no camps (Petrichor&#x27;s database)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Shaded_Dunes\">Wiki: Shaded Dunes</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Sungreet Strand (north gate): Ashira warriors 6-7, giant fire beetles 7-8, a hired thug 9-10 at Ameen Farm. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Sungreet_Strand\">Wiki: Sungreet Strand</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Night Harbor docks: goblin troublemakers (9) and squatters (10). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Night_Harbor\">Wiki: Night Harbor (rev 83168, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Infested Crypt (wiki 8-16, off Shaded Dunes): crypt guardians, creepers and spiderlings 8-9, broodmistress 10-12. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Infested_Crypt\">Wiki: Infested Crypt</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-bracer\"><summary><b>Ashira Warrior Bracer Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Tattered Rawhide plus Steel Talons faction; the bracer is an uncommon drop.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Watch Captain Badawi</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor · Watch Captain Badawi roams the upper garrison; turn in to Quartermaster Obaid</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Steel Talons (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); Tattered Rawhide</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Watch Captain Badawi wanders all about the upper garrison area of the city.</li><li>Quartermaster Obaid is located in the Garrison (near west gate) in Night Harbor, in a room adjacent to the area with soldiers hitting training dummies.</li><li>Quartermaster Obaid is looking for Ashira Warrior Bracer. These are an uncommon drop from an ashira warrior and other higher level ashira fighters.</li><li>Give Ashira Warrior Bracer to Quartermaster Obaid.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Tattered Rawhide from Quartermaster Obaid.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Steel Talons (+)</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ashira_Warrior_Bracer_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-ashira-warrior-bracer-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-12</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Night Terror (8): <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-winged\"><summary><b>A Winged Terror</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Kill the Night Terror (8), which spawns at night in the Necropolis yard, so come back at 8+.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Witcher Sayyaad</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>Necklace of Night</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Witcher Sayyaad is located in the Necropolis found within Night Harbor. Enter the Necropolis from the south entrance with the purple &quot;Concourse of Souls&quot; banner and immediately turn right.</li><li>Kill Night Terror, a level 8 named bat that spawns only at night in the Necropolis Courtyard and Saltbreeze Park areas of Night Harbor.</li><li>Night Terror will drop one of three items randomly, which can be returned to Witcher Sayyaad for a reward.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Mantle of Night</b></li><li>Loot Night Terror&#x27;s Wing from Night Terror.</li><li>Return to Witcher Sayyadd and hand him Night Terror&#x27;s Wing.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Mantle of Night from Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Tunic of Night</b></li><li>Loot Night Terror&#x27;s Fur from Night Terror.</li><li>Give Night Terror&#x27;s Fur to Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Tunic of Night from Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Necklace of Night</b></li><li>Loot Night Terror&#x27;s Head from Night Terror.</li><li>Give Night Terror&#x27;s Head to Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Necklace of Night from Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The reward is listed two ways: the walkthrough says Necklace of Night, and the Night Harbor quest table says Mantle of Night and Tunic of Night. Not resolved. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Night_Harbor\">Wiki: Night Harbor (rev 83168, 2026-10-18)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_Winged_Terror\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-a-winged-terror\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-09-30</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Jacobin Yeats): L6 Net Shot; L7 Flare, Snaring Shot; L8 Interrupting Shot, Strafing Barrage I; L9 Piercing Shot I; L10 Alarm Trap, Point Blank II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Jamee Langris): L6 Chant of Purity; L7 Repel; L8 Lento&#x27;s Aria of Stillness, Vellicosa&#x27;s Fanfare; L9 Languid Lullaby; L10 Dissonant Vocalization. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Leila Ghasem): L6 Pounce; L7 Chop I; L8 Remedy Companion, Savage Spirit; L9 Command: Kill; L10 Enraging Strike II, Maul I. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Dalinder Grammanoot): L8 Dispel Magic, Fear the Dead, Heal, Invisibility versus Undead, Lesser Redemption, Poison Protection, Promise of Mending I, Rebuke III, Resilience, Sense Magic, Shackle, Summon Food. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Rolan Talmula): L8 Cure Disease, Mantle of Summer, Mantle of Winter, Prickly Barrier, Sense Magic, Speed of the Wild, Summer&#x27;s Warmth, Summon Drink, Summon Food, Swarm of Mites, Twisting Roots, Winter&#x27;s Chill. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Tenebrim Tam): L8 Companion Strike II, Dispel Magic, Flame Shield, Minor Creation: Fire, Summon Arrows, Summon Minor Manastone, Summon Minor Water Trident, Summon Throwing Dagger. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Master Wincog): L8 Enchant Tin Bar, Illusion: Ogre, Lesser Enlightenment, Lesser Group Enlightenment, Lesser Vespyra&#x27;s Veil, Magic Protection, Minor Strength, Root, Runeskin, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Fedamius Steele III): L6 Armor Break; L7 Distracting Taunt; L8 Clobber, Intimidation; L9 Challenging Arrow I; L10 Rend II, Shield Bash I. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Petra Gyle): L6 Silence, Ward of Suspicion; L7 Fire Protection; L8 Censuring Strike II, Dominate the Mind, Pillage Mana, Sense Magic; L9 Dispel Magic; L10 Purifying Blow, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Chahaya Tam): L6 Sneak; L7 Pinning Throw; L9 Stone Stance; L10 Round Kick II. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Marvion Hallows, then Sekhmet): L8 Aspect of Vampirism, Blood Pact, Dispel Magic, Eye of the Underworld, Feign Death (Spell), Holy Protection, Invisibility, Lesser Unliving Shield, Life Drain II, Pact of Deathly Enduring, Poisonous Deluge, Rot Flesh, Summon Minor Lifestone, Terrify the Dead. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Trey Fulton): L6 Invisibility versus Undead; L7 Shield Toss; L8 Crusader Strike II, Fear the Dead, Healing Touch, Lay on Hands; L9 Blind; L10 Cure Poison, Restorative Smite. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Foss Dunestrider): L6 Swift Shot; L7 Invisibility versus Beasts; L8 Minor Mantle of the Hunter, Shroud, Taunt; L9 Barbed Shot, Twisting Roots; L10 Hunter&#x27;s Focus, Rending Cut, Survivor Stance. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Sinastin Aspenleaf): L6 Slice I; L7 Uppercut; L8 Sap; L9 Poison Tolerance; L10 Stab II. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Exavius Deathwhisper): L6 Grip of Shadow; L7 Cold Protection, Holy Protection; L8 Grip of Agony, Shadow Strike II, Siphoning Slash, Soul Servant, Soulrend II; L10 Aura of the Unholy, Lord of Shadows, Pulling Shadows, Reave, Terror in the Shadows. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Errol Shrewtender): L8 Ancestor&#x27;s Eye, Ghostly Blight, Greater Malady, Invisibility versus Undead, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Pact of Haste, Pact of Renewal, Purge, Speed of the Wild, Spirit Bane III, Spirit Mending, Summon Food. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Njau Hansou): L6 Magic Protection; L7 Phase Strike; L8 Conduit, Dispel Magic; L9 Electricity Protection; L10 Discharge, Electric Infusion, Infused Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Olvin Viscus): L8 Blink, Dispel Magic, Glyph: Mun, Insidious Magic, Lesser Spellshield, Minor Arcane Surge, Minor Iceblast, Sorcerous Mind, Spell Catalyst, Summon Mage Light. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"underdocks\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Underdocks · levels 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 6–10: Wererats, greater shadowbones, Deepcut bounties</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Wererat encampment along the north wall from the newbie gate: plaguespreaders 8-12, the rest 10-12; the easiest wererats are 5-8 (Fight Club walkthrough). Greater shadowbones 7-9, smugglers 9-10. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Underdocks\">Wiki: Underdocks (rev 82552, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Wererat_Fight_Club\">Wiki: Wererat Fight Club (rev 81100)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Deepcut bandit camps (5-8 camps of 4-5) east of North Gate East, past the wererats. The faction page calls them 10-16 and mostly group content; the named Belot spawns at any camp or in the mine. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Deepcut_Bandits\">Wiki faction: Deepcut Bandits</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Bounty (from 8 on the zone table): <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-bounty\"><summary><b>Deepcut Bandit Bounty</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> 8 silver plus XP and Descendian Order and Citizens of Underdocks faction per 6 Deepcut Bandit&#x27;s Hands. Group content at 10-16.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Traven Keldress</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks · Traven Keldress takes the hands; Elara Venn, the paymaster, redeems the receipt at the East Docks Bounty Office</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>The Descendian Order (+); Citizens of Underdocks (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); (money:8,0)</td></tr></table><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Deepcut Bandit&#x27;s Hand x6</b>: Deepcut bandits (miners 3-5, overseers 5-6, marksmen and others) at the 5-8 camps east of North Gate East, past the wererats</li></ul><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: The Descendian Order (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Underdocks (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Deepcut_Bandit_Bounty\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-deepcut-bandit-bounty\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-10</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional bounties: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-mush\"><summary><b>Mushroom Farmers Bounty Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Repeatable coin (the wiki says 2 silver, the walkthrough 1) plus Descendian Order and Citizens faction.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Mikra Velrane</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>The Descendian Order (+); Citizens of Underdocks (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); (money:1,0)</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: The Descendian Order (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Underdocks (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> Coin differs: 2 silver on the Underdocks quest table, 1 silver in the walkthrough. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Underdocks\">Wiki: Underdocks (rev 82552, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mushroom_Farmers_Bounty_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-mushroom-farmers-bounty-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-04</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-thieves\"><summary><b>Thieves Guild Bounty Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Repeatable 1 silver plus Descendian Order and Citizens faction.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Mikra Velrane</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>The Descendian Order (+); Citizens of Underdocks (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); (money:1,0)</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Reward</b></li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: The Descendian Order (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Underdocks (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Thieves_Guild_Bounty_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-thieves-guild-bounty-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-04</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-arson\"><summary><b>The Small Problem of Deepcut Arsonists</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl ?</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> 1 silver plus faction. Arsonists are an uncommon spawn in the Deepcut mining cave, and their oil is an uncommon drop.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Guard Darek</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>not listed</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive Small Storage Box from Guard Darek.; You receive 1 silver from Guard Darek.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Small Storage Box from Guard Darek.</li><li>Kill a Deepcut arsonist to collect 6 Vial of Flammable Oil. Arsonists are an uncommon spawn in the Deepcut mining cave, and the oils are an uncommon drop from them.</li><li>Combine the 6 oils within the box to craft Box of Oils.</li><li>Turn in the box to Guard Darek.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive 1 silver from Guard Darek.</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Small_Problem_of_Deepcut_Arsonists\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-the-small-problem-of-deepcut-arsonists\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-07</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Surface alternative: Shaded Dunes smugglers and wererats beach party (6-9, Toma the Two-Faced) and the Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane entrance (group 4-14), both through Night Harbor. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monme.no/camps\">monme.no camps (Petrichor&#x27;s database)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional, House Varros faction: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-syrsil\"><summary><b>Syrsil&#x27;s Stolen Package</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl ?</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> XP and House Varros faction (a Deep Elf house). Senior Apprentice Syrsil is in the Inn tavern.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Senior Apprentice Syrsil</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>not listed</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>You gain experience!</li><li>Your faction standing with House Varros got better.</li><li>Senior Apprentice Syrsil says, &quot;Varsa ai Neth&#x27;xan! The Shadow must have sent you to me. Perhaps I am destined for greatness after all.&quot;</li><li>Senior Apprentice Syrsil says, &quot;May you hear.&quot;</li><li>Senior Apprentice Syrsil nods at you appreciatively.</li><li>*</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Syrsil%27s_Stolen_Package\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-syrsils-stolen-package\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-14</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Simrut the Green (after Marshal Harding)): L6 Net Shot; L7 Flare, Snaring Shot; L8 Interrupting Shot, Strafing Barrage I; L9 Piercing Shot I; L10 Alarm Trap, Point Blank II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Crescindy (sells Bard songs)): L6 Chant of Purity; L7 Repel; L8 Lento&#x27;s Aria of Stillness, Vellicosa&#x27;s Fanfare; L9 Languid Lullaby; L10 Dissonant Vocalization. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Gunder Dinnig (after Marshal Harding)): L6 Pounce; L7 Chop I; L8 Remedy Companion, Savage Spirit; L9 Command: Kill; L10 Enraging Strike II, Maul I. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Sister Marwen (trainer); Soren Akedd starts the quest): L8 Dispel Magic, Fear the Dead, Heal, Invisibility versus Undead, Lesser Redemption, Poison Protection, Promise of Mending I, Rebuke III, Resilience, Sense Magic, Shackle, Summon Food. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Luskmit): L8 Cure Disease, Mantle of Summer, Mantle of Winter, Prickly Barrier, Sense Magic, Speed of the Wild, Summer&#x27;s Warmth, Summon Drink, Summon Food, Swarm of Mites, Twisting Roots, Winter&#x27;s Chill. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L8 Companion Strike II, Dispel Magic, Flame Shield, Minor Creation: Fire, Summon Arrows, Summon Minor Manastone, Summon Minor Water Trident, Summon Throwing Dagger. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L8 Enchant Tin Bar, Illusion: Ogre, Lesser Enlightenment, Lesser Group Enlightenment, Lesser Vespyra&#x27;s Veil, Magic Protection, Minor Strength, Root, Runeskin, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Gunder Dinnig (after Marshal Harding)): L6 Armor Break; L7 Distracting Taunt; L8 Clobber, Intimidation; L9 Challenging Arrow I; L10 Rend II, Shield Bash I. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Silence, Ward of Suspicion; L7 Fire Protection; L8 Censuring Strike II, Dominate the Mind, Pillage Mana, Sense Magic; L9 Dispel Magic; L10 Purifying Blow, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Sneak; L7 Pinning Throw; L9 Stone Stance; L10 Round Kick II. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Soren Akedd (starter quest)): L8 Aspect of Vampirism, Blood Pact, Dispel Magic, Eye of the Underworld, Feign Death (Spell), Holy Protection, Invisibility, Lesser Unliving Shield, Life Drain II, Pact of Deathly Enduring, Poisonous Deluge, Rot Flesh, Summon Minor Lifestone, Terrify the Dead. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Invisibility versus Undead; L7 Shield Toss; L8 Crusader Strike II, Fear the Dead, Healing Touch, Lay on Hands; L9 Blind; L10 Cure Poison, Restorative Smite. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Simrut the Green (after Marshal Harding)): L6 Swift Shot; L7 Invisibility versus Beasts; L8 Minor Mantle of the Hunter, Shroud, Taunt; L9 Barbed Shot, Twisting Roots; L10 Hunter&#x27;s Focus, Rending Cut, Survivor Stance. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Slylara Llumare): L6 Slice I; L7 Uppercut; L8 Sap; L9 Poison Tolerance; L10 Stab II. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Father Fyod (after Soren Akedd)): L6 Grip of Shadow; L7 Cold Protection, Holy Protection; L8 Grip of Agony, Shadow Strike II, Siphoning Slash, Soul Servant, Soulrend II; L10 Aura of the Unholy, Lord of Shadows, Pulling Shadows, Reave, Terror in the Shadows. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Picci Manifold): L8 Ancestor&#x27;s Eye, Ghostly Blight, Greater Malady, Invisibility versus Undead, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Pact of Haste, Pact of Renewal, Purge, Speed of the Wild, Spirit Bane III, Spirit Mending, Summon Food. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Magic Protection; L7 Phase Strike; L8 Conduit, Dispel Magic; L9 Electricity Protection; L10 Discharge, Electric Infusion, Infused Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L8 Blink, Dispel Magic, Glyph: Mun, Insidious Magic, Lesser Spellshield, Minor Arcane Surge, Minor Iceblast, Sorcerous Mind, Spell Catalyst, Summon Mage Light. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div></div>";window.MNM_QUICK.routenh["6-10"]="<div class=\"sc-wrap\"><p class=\"sc-pick\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> No start city picked: choose one in the <b>Start</b> box in the top bar to see its route for levels 6–10.</p><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"ailvorith\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Ail&#x27;Vorith · levels 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 6–10: Fungal armor, House quest Part 1, Blind Midden top floor</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor monk\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor, Monk only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Start your class House quest with your Obsidian Shackle (Obsidian Academy or Military Outpost). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-xal\"><summary><b>House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl Part 1: 8+, Part 2: 13+</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest: chest armor at 8, city access, House Xal&#x27;tharn faction and the Iron Render weapon.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Klavel Sul</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Foreign Quarter, Military Outpost: the building on the left past the bridge and gate, back of the room with the melee trainers (the quest page calls it the Obsidian Academy; see the Monk trainer note)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Part 1: 8+, Part 2: 13+</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Inquisitor, Monk</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>Obsidian Shackle from the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest. Deep Common language.</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Part 1 grants city access (wiki). Part 2 turn-in: &#x27;You gain faction with House Xal&#x27;tharn&#x27;. Other faction hits are marked as unknown on the wiki: no sourced data yet.</td></tr></table><h5>Steps <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h5><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Part 1 (8+): hail Klavel Sul; say &#x27;The Queen&#x27;, then &#x27;I would be a cenobite&#x27;, then &#x27;Do you have a task for me?&#x27;. You receive the Remnant Satchel (6 slots).</li><li>Swim around the west of the city, where elementals and skulls patrol the west island shores. Kill a separated skull and a spectral remnant (both 8-11) for 6 Lost Skull.</li><li>Combine the satchel and hand it to Klavel Sul (XP). Say &#x27;I swear allegiance to the Queen!&#x27; (XP). Inquisitors receive the Dull Iron Cuirass; Monks the Simple Chestwrap.</li><li>Part 2 (13+): before 13, Klavel says you lack the skill. At 13, hail him and say &#x27;I accept.&#x27; He gives a summons for Lady Miniel in the Shol&#x27;tar, beneath the Queen&#x27;s arena: take the road on the right into the Dark City and go through the dungeon gates near the bank.</li><li>Give the summons to Miniel Ubast in the Inquisitor&#x27;s Guildhall (NPC page: enter the main city, turn right, up the ramp, the prison guarded by Inquisitors, up one floor and through the door). Ask about the duty and where the exiles are.</li><li>Go to the exile camps to the south, by the river into the Great Cavern Sea: past the waterfall where snakes gather, on the bottom floor past the invisible hired thug. Kill exiles until you have one each of the Unknown, Silver and Gold Sigil of a Lesser House (unique: one of each).</li><li>Keep killing the bottom-floor exiles until Gullach Otal&#x27;qar (16-17, named Fighter) spawns in their place, then kill him for Gullach&#x27;s Head.</li><li>Hand the 3 sigils and the head to Miniel Ubast.</li></ol><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Lost Skull x6</b>: a separated skull (8-11, Enchanter: Mesmerize, Silence), a spectral remnant (8-11, Fighter), west island shores</li><li><b>Sigil of a Lesser House (Unknown, Silver, Gold)</b>: exiles: a starving outcast, a runaway, a praying exile (exile mobs are 15-22)</li><li><b>Gullach&#x27;s Head</b>: Gullach Otal&#x27;qar (16-17), bottom floor of the exile area behind the hired thug</li></ul><p><b>Turn in:</b> Part 1: Klavel Sul. Part 2: Miniel Ubast (Shol&#x27;tar, inside the city)</p><p><b>Rewards:</b> XP: XP at both Part 1 turn-ins and at the Part 2 turn-in · Item: Inquisitor: Dull Iron Cuirass (chest AC 9, STA +1, INT +1, HP +5) and Iron Render (1H slash 7/30, STR +2, STA +1, INT +1, HP +5, Mana +5). Monk: Simple Chestwrap and Tarnished Iron Bo. · Coin: none listed · Faction: City access (Part 1); House Xal&#x27;tharn + (Part 2)</p><p><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Reward conflict resolved, Cuirass wins. The quest page listed a Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant from its first version (2026-09-23, beta 0.30.0.0) until rev 78132 (2026-10-07, after the 0.30.2.1 release patch), when an editor replaced it with the Dull Iron Cuirass for Inquisitors. That editor created the Dull Iron Cuirass item page with full stats four minutes later. The Pendant item page was last touched 2026-09-26, and the Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests summary page that still says Pendant was never updated. The newer first-hand edit with an item page wins over the older summary. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)&amp;action=history\">Wiki edit history: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Dull_Iron_Cuirass\">Wiki: Dull Iron Cuirass (item page created 2026-10-07)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Xal%27tharn_Pendant\">Wiki: Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant (item page, last edited 2026-09-26)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span></p><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> Whether Monks (or pre-release characters) still get the Pendant as well: no sourced data yet. No talk page exists for the quest. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Xal%27tharn_Pendant\">Wiki: Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant (item page, last edited 2026-09-26)</a></span></p><p><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Do Part 2 at about 15-17, not 13: the sigil exiles are 15-22 and Gullach is 16-17 (wiki levels). Bring a group or a healer. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-xaltharn-quest\">quest helper</a> · <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Klavel_Sul\">Wiki: Klavel Sul (rev 82871, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Miniel_Ubast\">Wiki: Miniel Ubast</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Sigil_of_a_Lesser_House_(Gold)\">Wiki: Sigil of a Lesser House (Gold)</a></span></p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric paladin\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric, Paladin only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-drez\"><summary><b>House Drezzorith (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 8+</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (city access, the Lexicon of Mysteries line for Clerics).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Zalethra Drezzorith</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>8+</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Cleric, Paladin</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>House of Drezzorith (+); Citizens of Ail&#x27;vorith (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive Small Burlap Pouch from Zalethra Drezzorith.; You receive Lexicon of Mysteries from Zalethra Drezzorith.; You receive Letter for Alarys from Zalethra Drezzorith.; You receive Empty Sample Box from Alarys Drezzorith.; You receive Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries from Alarys Drezzorith.; You receive Advanced Lexicon of Mysteries from Tal Drezzorith.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>House Acceptance</b></li><li>Zalethra Drezzorith is located in the Obsidian Academy upper floor. From the bridge and gate into the Foreign Quarter, enter the building straight ahead with caster trainers and go upstairs.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Small Burlap Pouch from Zalethra Drezzorith.</li><li>Cross the bridge and turn right at the Toilmaster. Follow the water&#x27;s edge until your reach a cave full of cultists. Kill an angry cultist, an agitated cultist, a cultist priestess to collect 7 Cultist Eye to fill the bag.</li><li>Combine the container into Filled Burlap Pouch and return it to Zalethra Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Lexicon of Mysteries from Zalethra Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Letter for Alarys from Zalethra Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: House of Drezzorith (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Ail&#x27;vorith (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Faction with House of Drezzorith increased to High Indifferent</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Faction with Citizens of Ail&#x27;vorith increased to High Amicably</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Goblin Samples</b></li><li>Alarys Drezzorith is located in a building in the main city of Ail&#x27;Vorith, 4th floor, south side... just southeast of the high level Paladin and Cleric trainers. You can see it on the left side standing on the main bridge leading into the city.</li><li>Hand Alarys Drezzorith your Letter to Alarys.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Empty Sample Box from Alarys Drezzorith.</li><li>Kill a Deepgulp warrior, a Deepgulp scavenger, a Deepgulp hunter, a Deepgulp berserker to collect 6 Sample of Mind Control Substance and combine them to create Full Sample Box.</li><li>(Alternately, you can complete the Thanetal&#x27;s Samples quest handing in 1 Deep Ale and 10 silver to acquire 6 Sample of Mind Control Substance.)</li><li>Hand Full Sample Box to Alarys Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Any faction hits? EXP?</li><li>Hand Lexicon of Mysteries to Alarys Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries from Alarys Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Any faction hits? EXP?</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Continuation - Part 2</b></li><li>Tal Drezzorith is located in the building next to Alarys Drezzorith, directly across from the cleric/paladin guild</li><li>Hand the Intermediate Lexicon of Mysteries in to Tal Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Advanced Lexicon of Mysteries from Tal Drezzorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Any follow-up breadcrumbs?</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Drezzorith_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-drezzorith-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-11</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter rogue\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter, Rogue only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-ith\"><summary><b>House Ith&#x27;vayen (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (belt reward, city access).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Enchanter, Rogue</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive a Letter to Aleyz.; You receive a Cloth Belt of Runes.; You receive a Leather Belt of Runes.; You receive a Roasted and Poisoned Fish.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - A Letter of Recommendation - Req. Lvl 1</b></li><li>Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen is located in the front left corner of the first floor of the caster hall in the Obsidian Academy.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: You do not have to use the teleport to complete the quest.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: You are teleported out of the city and to the left across the bridge, up the ramp and to the right (most of the way to the zone safe point).</li><li>Upon turning in eight Myconid Parts:</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive a Letter to Aleyz.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive a Cloth Belt of Runes.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive a Leather Belt of Runes.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 2 - A Letter of Recommendation - Req. Lvl 1</b></li><li>Begins when you turn in a Letter to Aleyz to Aleyz Ith&#x27;vayen inside the main city.</li><li>Bring one Fire Elemental Stone, three Sample of Tainted Water and one Whitefish to Aleyz.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive a Roasted and Poisoned Fish.</li><li>Return to Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen. Stealth behind her and use the MUD commands /look table.</li><li>While holding the Roasted and Poisoned Fish use the MUD command /place table.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: As of 2026-10-12, this MUD command appears to be bugged and is not triggering correctly.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: More information is required...</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Ith%27vayen_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-ithvayen-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-12</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade wizard\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade, Wizard only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-hal\"><summary><b>House Hal&#x27;kareth (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (Hal&#x27;kareth Signet Ring).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Myal Vehear</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Spellblade, Wizard</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - ?</b></li><li>Myal Vehear is located in the Obsidian Academy, 2nd floor.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>a note for vhaleth hal&#x27;kareth</b></li><li class=\"dim\">Note: More information is required...</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Hal%27kareth_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-halkareth-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-10</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer ranger\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Archer, Ranger only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-vael\"><summary><b>House Vael&#x27;xirith (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Laren Drin&#x27;dar</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Archer, Ranger</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive Scalp Pouch from Laren Drin&#x27;dar.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - Goblin Scalps</b></li><li>Laren is located in the Military Outpost with the melee class instructors. From the bridge and gate into the Foreign Quarter, enter the building across, second on the left (not the bank tunnel). He is on the right, near back of the room.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Scalp Pouch from Laren Drin&#x27;dar.</li><li>Go kill a bunch of goblins and return.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Faction hits? Follow-up? Reward? Related NPCs?</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Vael%27xirith_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-vaelxirith-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-13</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist necromancer\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist, Necromancer only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-varros\"><summary><b>House Varros (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (House Varros faction).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Vaslir Naiyth</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Elementalist, Necromancer</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>House Varros (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); House Varros;</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1</b></li><li>Vaslir Naiyth is located in the Obsidian Academy. As you enter the academy, she is located near the stairs in the back of the room on the right.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: House Varros (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: House Varros (+)</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 2</b></li><li>Vaslir Vharkith is located near the top of Ail&#x27;Vorith proper, next to some other Vaslir NPCs.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Find the Escaped Slave</b></li><li>Although Laeran Birchshade cons as &quot;Ready to attack&quot;, he does not attack on sight. He may either be killed for Vharkith&#x27;s Research Notes or spoken with instead. Speaking with him also begins a separate optional quest involving the Birchshade Family Bracelet. See Laeran Birchshade for details.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Speak with Vaslir Maryn</b></li><li>Vaslir Maryn is located near Vaslir Vharkith in the upper area of Ail&#x27;Vorith, standing beside the large fountain. Vaslir Kiannes is also located nearby.</li><li>At this point there are two confirmed routes for obtaining Flask of Essairyl. You may gather elemental essences for Vaslir Maryn, or speak with Vaslir Kiannes and complete his water-sample task instead. You only need to complete one route.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Gather the Elemental Essences =</b></li><li>4 Essence of Elemental Air</li><li>4 Essence of Elemental Earth</li><li>Only the Air and Earth elementals are needed for this step. Water elementals can also be found around the shores near Ail&#x27;Vorith proper, but they do not provide the essences Maryn requests.</li><li>There are also Water elementals along the shoreline surrounding the city. Make sure you are hunting Air Elementals and Earth Elementals for this quest.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Return to Vaslir Maryn =</b></li><li>4 Essence of Elemental Air</li><li>4 Essence of Elemental Earth</li><li>the Corpse Dust given to you by Vaslir Vharkith</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Route B: Earn Essairyl from Vaslir Kiannes</b></li><li>Vaslir Kiannes is located near Vaslir Maryn and Vaslir Vharkith in the upper area of Ail&#x27;Vorith, near the fountain.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Gather the Water Samples =</b></li><li>10 Sample of Tainted Water</li><li>Corpse Dust</li><li>This is an alternative to gathering Essence of Elemental Air and Essence of Elemental Earth for Vaslir Maryn. You do not need to complete both routes.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: House Varros (+)</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Obtain Nerolir</b></li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Purchase Nerolir from Miral =</b></li><li>The exact item name and item details for Nerolir still need to be verified from the in-game item window.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Return Nerolir to Vaslir Vharkith =</b></li><li>The exact hand-in dialogue, experience reward, faction change, and any other reward from the Nerolir turn-in still need to be confirmed.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>The Note and the Order</b></li><li>It still needs to be confirmed whether receiving the Letter to Freysia Riftrend also awards experience or House Varros faction.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Retrieve Vharkith&#x27;s Order =</b></li><li>Vharkith&#x27;s Order</li><li>Belot&#x27;s exact location, level, NPC class, spawn conditions, and complete loot table still need to be documented. It should also be confirmed whether Vharkith&#x27;s Order is a guaranteed drop.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>= Return Vharkith&#x27;s Order =</b></li><li>The dialogue, experience reward, faction change, item rewards, and continuation of the quest after returning Vharkith&#x27;s Order still need to be documented.</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Varros_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-varros-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-10</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> House quest for your class: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-velg\"><summary><b>House Velgarrith (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest (Frayed Cloak of House Velgarrith).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Xilonen Velgarrith</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Shadow Knight</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - Req. Lvl 2</b></li><li>Xilonen Velgarrith is located upstairs in the martial trainer building</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: More information is required...</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Velgarrith_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-velgarrith-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-13</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> From level 5: farm cave myconids (5-7) for the Fungal Armor Quests. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Armor_Quests\">Wiki: Fungal Armor Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-fungal\"><summary><b>Fungal Armor Quests</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 5</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Four armor pieces for 14 classes, including Inquisitor, plus Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith faction toward banking and vendors.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Leatherworker Vex</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Foreign Trader&#x27;s Market, Foreign Quarter</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>5</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>Deep Common language. The class list on the items is ARC BRD BST CLR DRU FTR INQ MNK PAL RNG ROG SHD SHM SPB (no pure casters).</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Each piece: House Velgarrith + and Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith + (wiki).</td></tr></table><h5>Steps <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h5><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Hail Leatherworker Vex, then ask &#x27;What is something that could keep me alive longer?&#x27; and say &#x27;I seek protection.&#x27;</li><li>Ask &#x27;What Coat?&#x27;, &#x27;What Helm?&#x27;, &#x27;What Leggings?&#x27; or &#x27;What Boots?&#x27; for each piece&#x27;s recipe.</li><li>Coat: 3 Perfect Fungus Cap, 2 Strong Fungus Hyphea, 1 Perfect Fungus Stem. Helm: 2 Cap, 1 Hyphea. Leggings: 2 Stem, 2 Hyphea, 2 Perfect Fungus Volva. Boots: 2 Volva, 2 Hyphea.</li><li>Hand each set of parts to Vex to receive that piece (XP and faction each).</li></ol><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Full set: 7 Strong Fungus Hyphea, 5 Perfect Fungus Cap, 4 Perfect Fungus Volva, 3 Perfect Fungus Stem</b>: a cave myconid (5-7)</li></ul><p><b>Turn in:</b> Leatherworker Vex</p><p><b>Rewards:</b> XP: Experience per piece · Item: Fungal Coat (AC 7), Fungal Helm (AC 5), Fungal Leggings (AC 6), Fungal Boots (AC 4) · Coin: none listed · Faction: House Velgarrith +, Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith +</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Armor_Quests\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-fungal-armor-quests\">quest helper</a> · <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Armor_Quests\">Wiki: Fungal Armor Quests</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Coat\">Wiki: Fungal Coat (class list)</a></span></p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Camps (wiki levels): a cave myconid 5-7, a bubbling oozeling 5-7, a Deepgulp runt and a Deepgulp explorer 6-7 (their kills raise Ail&#x27;vorith Exiles), a skeleton 6-7, a cave snake 7-9, cultists 6-7 (cave along the water&#x27;s edge, right of the Toilmaster). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27vorith_Exiles\">Wiki faction: Ail&#x27;vorith Exiles</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Drezzorith_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Drezzorith (Quest)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor monk\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor, Monk only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> At 8+: the west island shores (swim around the west of the city) have a separated skull and a spectral remnant (8-11) for Xal&#x27;tharn Part 1, plus elementals and spirits (9-11). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Blind Midden top floor: 6-7 prisoners and outcasts, and named mobs at level 7 (Gorgeous, Flavic the Fisher, Mucky Morgurah, Forager Davra, Sethrine the Unblinking) with gear drops. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Blind_Midden\">Wiki: Blind Midden (rev 83212)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-merit\"><summary><b>Mark of Merit</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1 (repeatable)</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> XP and Marks of Merit for the Midden Mark Menu while you clear Blind Midden named mobs.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Blind Midden ground floor (map point 1)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1 (repeatable)</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>None listed.</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><h5>Steps <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h5><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Kill any named mob in Blind Midden and loot its corpse item (no drop).</li><li>Turn the corpse in to Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra.</li></ol><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Corpse of &lt;named&gt;</b>: any Blind Midden named (top floor named are 7-12, basement named 15+)</li></ul><p><b>Turn in:</b> Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra</p><p><b>Rewards:</b> XP: Experience · Item: Blind Midden Mark of Merit (Midden Mark Menu rewards are random) · Coin: none listed · Faction: no sourced data yet</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mark_of_Merit\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-mark-of-merit\">quest helper</a> · <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mark_of_Merit\">Wiki: Mark of Merit</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Blind_Midden\">Wiki: Blind Midden (rev 83212)</a></span></p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor only</span> <span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Order: fungal pieces while you level on myconids (5-8), then Xal&#x27;tharn Part 1 at 8-9 for the Dull Iron Cuirass and city access. Visit Nurvol Cereveth every time you reach a spell level. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Fungal_Armor_Quests\">Wiki: Fungal Armor Quests</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Lurithos Kest): L6 Net Shot; L7 Flare, Snaring Shot; L8 Interrupting Shot, Strafing Barrage I; L9 Piercing Shot I; L10 Alarm Trap, Point Blank II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Chant of Purity; L7 Repel; L8 Lento&#x27;s Aria of Stillness, Vellicosa&#x27;s Fanfare; L9 Languid Lullaby; L10 Dissonant Vocalization. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Pounce; L7 Chop I; L8 Remedy Companion, Savage Spirit; L9 Command: Kill; L10 Enraging Strike II, Maul I. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Zalethra Drezzorith): L8 Dispel Magic, Fear the Dead, Heal, Invisibility versus Undead, Lesser Redemption, Poison Protection, Promise of Mending I, Rebuke III, Resilience, Sense Magic, Shackle, Summon Food. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Cure Disease, Mantle of Summer, Mantle of Winter, Prickly Barrier, Sense Magic, Speed of the Wild, Summer&#x27;s Warmth, Summon Drink, Summon Food, Swarm of Mites, Twisting Roots, Winter&#x27;s Chill. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Lothur Varros): L8 Companion Strike II, Dispel Magic, Flame Shield, Minor Creation: Fire, Summon Arrows, Summon Minor Manastone, Summon Minor Water Trident, Summon Throwing Dagger. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen): L8 Enchant Tin Bar, Illusion: Ogre, Lesser Enlightenment, Lesser Group Enlightenment, Lesser Vespyra&#x27;s Veil, Magic Protection, Minor Strength, Root, Runeskin, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Tharkan Inathar): L6 Armor Break; L7 Distracting Taunt; L8 Clobber, Intimidation; L9 Challenging Arrow I; L10 Rend II, Shield Bash I. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Nurvol Cereveth): L6 Silence, Ward of Suspicion; L7 Fire Protection; L8 Censuring Strike II, Dominate the Mind, Pillage Mana, Sense Magic; L9 Dispel Magic; L10 Purifying Blow, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Klavel Sul): L6 Sneak; L7 Pinning Throw; L9 Stone Stance; L10 Round Kick II. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vaslir Naiyth): L8 Aspect of Vampirism, Blood Pact, Dispel Magic, Eye of the Underworld, Feign Death (Spell), Holy Protection, Invisibility, Lesser Unliving Shield, Life Drain II, Pact of Deathly Enduring, Poisonous Deluge, Rot Flesh, Summon Minor Lifestone, Terrify the Dead. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Mentvar Drezzorith): L6 Invisibility versus Undead; L7 Shield Toss; L8 Crusader Strike II, Fear the Dead, Healing Touch, Lay on Hands; L9 Blind; L10 Cure Poison, Restorative Smite. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Laren Drin&#x27;dar): L6 Swift Shot; L7 Invisibility versus Beasts; L8 Minor Mantle of the Hunter, Shroud, Taunt; L9 Barbed Shot, Twisting Roots; L10 Hunter&#x27;s Focus, Rending Cut, Survivor Stance. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Zorvanna Velgarrith): L6 Slice I; L7 Uppercut; L8 Sap; L9 Poison Tolerance; L10 Stab II. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vhalrek Velgarrith): L6 Grip of Shadow; L7 Cold Protection, Holy Protection; L8 Grip of Agony, Shadow Strike II, Siphoning Slash, Soul Servant, Soulrend II; L10 Aura of the Unholy, Lord of Shadows, Pulling Shadows, Reave, Terror in the Shadows. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Ancestor&#x27;s Eye, Ghostly Blight, Greater Malady, Invisibility versus Undead, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Pact of Haste, Pact of Renewal, Purge, Speed of the Wild, Spirit Bane III, Spirit Mending, Summon Food. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Ilnara Hal&#x27;kareth): L6 Magic Protection; L7 Phase Strike; L8 Conduit, Dispel Magic; L9 Electricity Protection; L10 Discharge, Electric Infusion, Infused Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vhasilla Hal&#x27;kareth): L8 Blink, Dispel Magic, Glyph: Mun, Insidious Magic, Lesser Spellshield, Minor Arcane Surge, Minor Iceblast, Sorcerous Mind, Spell Catalyst, Summon Mage Light. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul><p class=\"sc-nhnote\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The class notes below were written for a <b>Night Harbor</b> start (Night Harbor gates, the Night Market forge, Night Harbor camps). You picked Ail&#x27;Vorith: use the route above for where to go.</p></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"faelindral\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Faelindral · levels 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 6–10: Fellstone orcs, wolf den, widows</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Fellstone orcs: warriors and necromancers 5-7, Fellstone shamans 7+, guards 8+, trackers 8-10, ragecallers 9+, defilers 10+. Named: Scout Leader Krindor (6, on the ridge past the Kennel Lift bridges) and Vorkuul Blighteye (7). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Beastmaster_Starter_Quest_(Faelindral)\">Wiki: Beastmaster Starter Quest (Faelindral) (rev 82724, 2026-10-17)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Wolves, west along the hillside path near the Druid Ring (solo 9, group 6-10; a good leather source): beguiled wolves ~7-8, a beguiled alpha wolf (8-10, named), and Rotmuzzle (9) with rabid wolves and skeletons. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Spiders: elder widows and widow matrons 7-8; Mezzatrian Boneweaver (7-9, a Necromancer spider). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Named: Kyros Emeraldscale (8, across the river west of the Newbie Lift bridge; drops the Poison Duct for the drakeling coat and pants). Fossergrim watchers 9-11, Meluli Dawnglow 8-12?. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Keeper&#x27;s Bight edge (by Evershade Weald): bight asps ~8-9, forest whelps 10-11, black bears 10-12. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Keeper%27s_Bight\">Wiki: Keeper&#x27;s Bight</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-faelindral-sixeyes\"><summary><b>Six Eyes Too Many</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Pixie Glitter (used in the Bard starter) for 6 Widow Eyes. Court of Summer + and Court of Winter −.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Polietta Two-tone</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Evershade Weald · Polietta Two-tone, up on the hill near the fae guardians (daytime only)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Court of Summer (+); Court of Winter (-)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>Pixie Glitter; (exp);</td></tr></table><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Widow Eye x6</b>: black widows (4-5) and elder widows (7-8)</li></ul><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Locate Polietta Two-tone, who spawns in Evershade Weald during the day up on the hill near the Fae Guardians.</li><li>Hunt a black widow and an elder widow until you have collected 6 x Widow Eye.</li><li>Hand 6 x Widow Eye to Polietta Two-tone.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Court of Summer (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Court of Winter (-)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Pixie Glitter from Polietta Two-tone.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Pixie Glitter is used for Bard Starter Quest (Faelindral).</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Six_Eyes_Too_Many\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-six-eyes-too-many\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-09-27</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional (long, travels to Night Harbor): <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-faelindral-sweet\"><summary><b>A Sweet Treat</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> A long chain from Faelindral to Night Harbor: Defenders, Citizens and Smallfolk Alliance faction, 55 silver in total, and the Stein of Baker&#x27;s Scorn. Starts with one Jelly Cupcake for Guard Pippi Pinecone.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Guard Pippi Pinecone</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Evershade Weald</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Defenders of Faelindral (+); Citizens of Faelindral (+); Smallfolk Alliance (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>Stein of Baker&#x27;s Scorn, 1; Half of a Jelly Cupcake, 1; (exp); (money: 55S)</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Note: Guard Pippi Pinecone has ambient dialogue that clues the observant player on how to initiate this quest.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>The Hungry Guard</b></li><li>Give Guard Pippi Pinecone 1 x Jelly Cupcake, which you can obtain from completing Mierra&#x27;s Famed Cupcakes.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Defenders of Faelindral (+)</li><li>Head to Mierra Willowshade near the inn.</li><li>Bring 12 x Royal Jelly and 1 x Satchel to Mierra Willowshade.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Faelindral (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Packaged Cupcakes from Mierra Willowshade.</li><li>Deliver 1 x Packaged Cupcakes to Guard Pippi Pinecone.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Packaged Cupcakes from Guard Pippi Pinecone.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Delivery</b></li><li>Travel to the Smallfolk District, south of Saltbreeze Park, in Night Harbor and search for Guard Halfsies. You can ask other guards in the area about Pete Pinecone as well.</li><li>Hand the Packaged Cupcakes to Guard Halfsies.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Smallfolk Alliance (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive {{Money 0 0 5 0</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Half of a Jelly Cupcake from Guard Halfsies.</li><li>Travel to Chef Violyn, who is located at the Crimson Oasis Inn near the North Gate of Night Harbor.</li><li>Hand the Half of a Jelly Cupcake to Chef Violyn.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Violyn&#x27;s Grocery Basket from Chef Violyn.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Violyn&#x27;s Grocery List from Chef Violyn.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>A Fiery Treat</b></li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Additional information regarding collection of the grocery list items would be beneficial.</li><li>Violyn&#x27;s Grocery List notes the required items, but not where to obtain them. Chef Violyn is not willing to help, either.</li><li>Purchase 2 x Dried Dragon&#x27;s Breath Pepper from Spices Merchant in Night Harbor.</li><li>Purchase 1 x Baladi from the Mukhtar Brewery in the river pirate tavern.</li><li>Purchase 4 x Basilisk Seasoning from An exotic cook in Shallow Shoals.</li><li>Purchase 2 x Viper&#x27;s Kick which can be obtained from the Viper&#x27;s Kick Recipe quest.</li><li>Combine 2 x Dried Dragon&#x27;s Breath Pepper, 1 x Baladi, 4 x Basilisk Seasoning, and 2 x Viper&#x27;s Kick in Violyn&#x27;s Grocery Basket.</li><li>Turn in Violyn&#x27;s Full Grocery Basket to Chef Violyn in Night Harbor.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Smallfolk Alliance (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Some of the following dialogue is incomplete and needs correction.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Violyn&#x27;s Special Batch of Cupcakes from Chef Violyn.</li><li>Give Violyn&#x27;s Special Batch of Cupcakes to Guard Halfsies.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Smallfolk Alliance (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Half of Violyn&#x27;s Cupcake from Guard Halfsies.</li><li>Give Half of Violyn&#x27;s Cupcake to Chef Violyn.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Smallfolk Alliance (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive {{Money 0 0 50 0</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Stein of Baker&#x27;s Scorn from Chef Violyn.</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest as needing more information. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_Sweet_Treat\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-a-sweet-treat\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-06</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Keyaryn Thornshade): L6 Net Shot; L7 Flare, Snaring Shot; L8 Interrupting Shot, Strafing Barrage I; L9 Piercing Shot I; L10 Alarm Trap, Point Blank II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Pine Brightreed (starter); Sylphrena Starfall and Laenyth Windharp): L6 Chant of Purity; L7 Repel; L8 Lento&#x27;s Aria of Stillness, Vellicosa&#x27;s Fanfare; L9 Languid Lullaby; L10 Dissonant Vocalization. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Relgen Greenblade, then Aerin Mossfang): L6 Pounce; L7 Chop I; L8 Remedy Companion, Savage Spirit; L9 Command: Kill; L10 Enraging Strike II, Maul I. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Dispel Magic, Fear the Dead, Heal, Invisibility versus Undead, Lesser Redemption, Poison Protection, Promise of Mending I, Rebuke III, Resilience, Sense Magic, Shackle, Summon Food. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (High Gatekeeper Sylvarya Starveil): L8 Cure Disease, Mantle of Summer, Mantle of Winter, Prickly Barrier, Sense Magic, Speed of the Wild, Summer&#x27;s Warmth, Summon Drink, Summon Food, Swarm of Mites, Twisting Roots, Winter&#x27;s Chill. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Companion Strike II, Dispel Magic, Flame Shield, Minor Creation: Fire, Summon Arrows, Summon Minor Manastone, Summon Minor Water Trident, Summon Throwing Dagger. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Enchant Tin Bar, Illusion: Ogre, Lesser Enlightenment, Lesser Group Enlightenment, Lesser Vespyra&#x27;s Veil, Magic Protection, Minor Strength, Root, Runeskin, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Vaelric Ironbark, then Craftguard Vinebrow): L6 Armor Break; L7 Distracting Taunt; L8 Clobber, Intimidation; L9 Challenging Arrow I; L10 Rend II, Shield Bash I. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Silence, Ward of Suspicion; L7 Fire Protection; L8 Censuring Strike II, Dominate the Mind, Pillage Mana, Sense Magic; L9 Dispel Magic; L10 Purifying Blow, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Sneak; L7 Pinning Throw; L9 Stone Stance; L10 Round Kick II. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Aspect of Vampirism, Blood Pact, Dispel Magic, Eye of the Underworld, Feign Death (Spell), Holy Protection, Invisibility, Lesser Unliving Shield, Life Drain II, Pact of Deathly Enduring, Poisonous Deluge, Rot Flesh, Summon Minor Lifestone, Terrify the Dead. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Invisibility versus Undead; L7 Shield Toss; L8 Crusader Strike II, Fear the Dead, Healing Touch, Lay on Hands; L9 Blind; L10 Cure Poison, Restorative Smite. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Relgen Greenblade): L6 Swift Shot; L7 Invisibility versus Beasts; L8 Minor Mantle of the Hunter, Shroud, Taunt; L9 Barbed Shot, Twisting Roots; L10 Hunter&#x27;s Focus, Rending Cut, Survivor Stance. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Elyndiir Nightshade): L6 Slice I; L7 Uppercut; L8 Sap; L9 Poison Tolerance; L10 Stab II. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Grip of Shadow; L7 Cold Protection, Holy Protection; L8 Grip of Agony, Shadow Strike II, Siphoning Slash, Soul Servant, Soulrend II; L10 Aura of the Unholy, Lord of Shadows, Pulling Shadows, Reave, Terror in the Shadows. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Varilis Thornvine): L8 Ancestor&#x27;s Eye, Ghostly Blight, Greater Malady, Invisibility versus Undead, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Pact of Haste, Pact of Renewal, Purge, Speed of the Wild, Spirit Bane III, Spirit Mending, Summon Food. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Magic Protection; L7 Phase Strike; L8 Conduit, Dispel Magic; L9 Electricity Protection; L10 Discharge, Electric Infusion, Infused Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L8 Blink, Dispel Magic, Glyph: Mun, Insidious Magic, Lesser Spellshield, Minor Arcane Surge, Minor Iceblast, Sorcerous Mind, Spell Catalyst, Summon Mage Light. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul><p class=\"sc-nhnote\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The class notes below were written for a <b>Night Harbor</b> start (Night Harbor gates, the Night Market forge, Night Harbor camps). You picked Faelindral: use the route above for where to go.</p></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"night-harbor\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Night Harbor · levels 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 6–10: Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane, Shaded Dunes Ashira, smuggler beach</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane (wiki 3-15), next to Night Harbor: skeletal fighters 3-10, warriors 4-11, cavaliers 6-10. Named Timmon Bell and Jakob Geffrey (~8), Lieutenant Gregan Snyde and Ariblast the Wicked (10). Hunting guide: solo 8, group 4-14, good gear drops. Player-tracked: most at 13. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Tomb_of_the_Last_Wyrmsbane\">Wiki: Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.wiki/zones/tomb-of-the-last-wyrmsbane\">monstersandmemories.wiki: Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane (player-tracked levels and coin)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Several class quests run through the Tomb: the Paladin starter (Engraved Coin upstairs), Wizard (4) and Necromancer and Shaman (8) steps. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Tomb_of_the_Last_Wyrmsbane\">Wiki: Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Shaded Dunes: the Ashira camps near the Tel Ekir zone line (group 6-10), with the zone line handy if pulls go wrong. Dhajr Spitemaw (8+) is at the large Ashira camp and raises Red Mantles. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Shaded_Dunes\">Wiki: Shaded Dunes</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Red_Mantles\">Wiki faction: Red Mantles</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Shaded Dunes smugglers and wererats beach party, the furthest camp west along the south coast (6-9), with Toma the Two-Faced (9+). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monme.no/camps\">monme.no camps (Petrichor&#x27;s database)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Shaded_Dunes\">Wiki: Shaded Dunes</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Sungreet Strand (north gate): Ashira warriors 6-7, giant fire beetles 7-8, a hired thug 9-10 at Ameen Farm. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Sungreet_Strand\">Wiki: Sungreet Strand</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Night Harbor docks: goblin troublemakers (9) and squatters (10). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Night_Harbor\">Wiki: Night Harbor (rev 83168, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Infested Crypt (wiki 8-16, off Shaded Dunes): crypt guardians, creepers and spiderlings 8-9, broodmistress 10-12. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Infested_Crypt\">Wiki: Infested Crypt</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-bracer\"><summary><b>Ashira Warrior Bracer Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Tattered Rawhide plus Steel Talons faction; the bracer is an uncommon drop.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Watch Captain Badawi</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor · Watch Captain Badawi roams the upper garrison; turn in to Quartermaster Obaid</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Steel Talons (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); Tattered Rawhide</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Watch Captain Badawi wanders all about the upper garrison area of the city.</li><li>Quartermaster Obaid is located in the Garrison (near west gate) in Night Harbor, in a room adjacent to the area with soldiers hitting training dummies.</li><li>Quartermaster Obaid is looking for Ashira Warrior Bracer. These are an uncommon drop from an ashira warrior and other higher level ashira fighters.</li><li>Give Ashira Warrior Bracer to Quartermaster Obaid.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Tattered Rawhide from Quartermaster Obaid.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Steel Talons (+)</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ashira_Warrior_Bracer_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-ashira-warrior-bracer-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-12</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Night Terror (8): <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-winged\"><summary><b>A Winged Terror</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Kill the Night Terror (8), which spawns at night in the Necropolis yard, so come back at 8+.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Witcher Sayyaad</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>Necklace of Night</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Witcher Sayyaad is located in the Necropolis found within Night Harbor. Enter the Necropolis from the south entrance with the purple &quot;Concourse of Souls&quot; banner and immediately turn right.</li><li>Kill Night Terror, a level 8 named bat that spawns only at night in the Necropolis Courtyard and Saltbreeze Park areas of Night Harbor.</li><li>Night Terror will drop one of three items randomly, which can be returned to Witcher Sayyaad for a reward.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Mantle of Night</b></li><li>Loot Night Terror&#x27;s Wing from Night Terror.</li><li>Return to Witcher Sayyadd and hand him Night Terror&#x27;s Wing.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Mantle of Night from Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Tunic of Night</b></li><li>Loot Night Terror&#x27;s Fur from Night Terror.</li><li>Give Night Terror&#x27;s Fur to Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Tunic of Night from Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Necklace of Night</b></li><li>Loot Night Terror&#x27;s Head from Night Terror.</li><li>Give Night Terror&#x27;s Head to Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Necklace of Night from Witcher Sayyaad.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The reward is listed two ways: the walkthrough says Necklace of Night, and the Night Harbor quest table says Mantle of Night and Tunic of Night. Not resolved. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Night_Harbor\">Wiki: Night Harbor (rev 83168, 2026-10-18)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_Winged_Terror\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-a-winged-terror\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-09-30</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Jacobin Yeats): L6 Net Shot; L7 Flare, Snaring Shot; L8 Interrupting Shot, Strafing Barrage I; L9 Piercing Shot I; L10 Alarm Trap, Point Blank II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Jamee Langris): L6 Chant of Purity; L7 Repel; L8 Lento&#x27;s Aria of Stillness, Vellicosa&#x27;s Fanfare; L9 Languid Lullaby; L10 Dissonant Vocalization. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Leila Ghasem): L6 Pounce; L7 Chop I; L8 Remedy Companion, Savage Spirit; L9 Command: Kill; L10 Enraging Strike II, Maul I. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Dalinder Grammanoot): L8 Dispel Magic, Fear the Dead, Heal, Invisibility versus Undead, Lesser Redemption, Poison Protection, Promise of Mending I, Rebuke III, Resilience, Sense Magic, Shackle, Summon Food. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Rolan Talmula): L8 Cure Disease, Mantle of Summer, Mantle of Winter, Prickly Barrier, Sense Magic, Speed of the Wild, Summer&#x27;s Warmth, Summon Drink, Summon Food, Swarm of Mites, Twisting Roots, Winter&#x27;s Chill. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Tenebrim Tam): L8 Companion Strike II, Dispel Magic, Flame Shield, Minor Creation: Fire, Summon Arrows, Summon Minor Manastone, Summon Minor Water Trident, Summon Throwing Dagger. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Master Wincog): L8 Enchant Tin Bar, Illusion: Ogre, Lesser Enlightenment, Lesser Group Enlightenment, Lesser Vespyra&#x27;s Veil, Magic Protection, Minor Strength, Root, Runeskin, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Fedamius Steele III): L6 Armor Break; L7 Distracting Taunt; L8 Clobber, Intimidation; L9 Challenging Arrow I; L10 Rend II, Shield Bash I. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Petra Gyle): L6 Silence, Ward of Suspicion; L7 Fire Protection; L8 Censuring Strike II, Dominate the Mind, Pillage Mana, Sense Magic; L9 Dispel Magic; L10 Purifying Blow, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Chahaya Tam): L6 Sneak; L7 Pinning Throw; L9 Stone Stance; L10 Round Kick II. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Marvion Hallows, then Sekhmet): L8 Aspect of Vampirism, Blood Pact, Dispel Magic, Eye of the Underworld, Feign Death (Spell), Holy Protection, Invisibility, Lesser Unliving Shield, Life Drain II, Pact of Deathly Enduring, Poisonous Deluge, Rot Flesh, Summon Minor Lifestone, Terrify the Dead. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Trey Fulton): L6 Invisibility versus Undead; L7 Shield Toss; L8 Crusader Strike II, Fear the Dead, Healing Touch, Lay on Hands; L9 Blind; L10 Cure Poison, Restorative Smite. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Foss Dunestrider): L6 Swift Shot; L7 Invisibility versus Beasts; L8 Minor Mantle of the Hunter, Shroud, Taunt; L9 Barbed Shot, Twisting Roots; L10 Hunter&#x27;s Focus, Rending Cut, Survivor Stance. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Sinastin Aspenleaf): L6 Slice I; L7 Uppercut; L8 Sap; L9 Poison Tolerance; L10 Stab II. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Exavius Deathwhisper): L6 Grip of Shadow; L7 Cold Protection, Holy Protection; L8 Grip of Agony, Shadow Strike II, Siphoning Slash, Soul Servant, Soulrend II; L10 Aura of the Unholy, Lord of Shadows, Pulling Shadows, Reave, Terror in the Shadows. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Errol Shrewtender): L8 Ancestor&#x27;s Eye, Ghostly Blight, Greater Malady, Invisibility versus Undead, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Pact of Haste, Pact of Renewal, Purge, Speed of the Wild, Spirit Bane III, Spirit Mending, Summon Food. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Njau Hansou): L6 Magic Protection; L7 Phase Strike; L8 Conduit, Dispel Magic; L9 Electricity Protection; L10 Discharge, Electric Infusion, Infused Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Olvin Viscus): L8 Blink, Dispel Magic, Glyph: Mun, Insidious Magic, Lesser Spellshield, Minor Arcane Surge, Minor Iceblast, Sorcerous Mind, Spell Catalyst, Summon Mage Light. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"underdocks\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Underdocks · levels 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 6–10: Wererats, greater shadowbones, Deepcut bounties</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Wererat encampment along the north wall from the newbie gate: plaguespreaders 8-12, the rest 10-12; the easiest wererats are 5-8 (Fight Club walkthrough). Greater shadowbones 7-9, smugglers 9-10. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Underdocks\">Wiki: Underdocks (rev 82552, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Wererat_Fight_Club\">Wiki: Wererat Fight Club (rev 81100)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Deepcut bandit camps (5-8 camps of 4-5) east of North Gate East, past the wererats. The faction page calls them 10-16 and mostly group content; the named Belot spawns at any camp or in the mine. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Deepcut_Bandits\">Wiki faction: Deepcut Bandits</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Bounty (from 8 on the zone table): <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-bounty\"><summary><b>Deepcut Bandit Bounty</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> 8 silver plus XP and Descendian Order and Citizens of Underdocks faction per 6 Deepcut Bandit&#x27;s Hands. Group content at 10-16.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Traven Keldress</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks · Traven Keldress takes the hands; Elara Venn, the paymaster, redeems the receipt at the East Docks Bounty Office</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>The Descendian Order (+); Citizens of Underdocks (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); (money:8,0)</td></tr></table><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Deepcut Bandit&#x27;s Hand x6</b>: Deepcut bandits (miners 3-5, overseers 5-6, marksmen and others) at the 5-8 camps east of North Gate East, past the wererats</li></ul><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: The Descendian Order (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Underdocks (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Deepcut_Bandit_Bounty\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-deepcut-bandit-bounty\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-10</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional bounties: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-mush\"><summary><b>Mushroom Farmers Bounty Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Repeatable coin (the wiki says 2 silver, the walkthrough 1) plus Descendian Order and Citizens faction.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Mikra Velrane</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>The Descendian Order (+); Citizens of Underdocks (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); (money:1,0)</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: The Descendian Order (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Underdocks (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> Coin differs: 2 silver on the Underdocks quest table, 1 silver in the walkthrough. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Underdocks\">Wiki: Underdocks (rev 82552, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mushroom_Farmers_Bounty_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-mushroom-farmers-bounty-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-04</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-thieves\"><summary><b>Thieves Guild Bounty Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Repeatable 1 silver plus Descendian Order and Citizens faction.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Mikra Velrane</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>The Descendian Order (+); Citizens of Underdocks (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); (money:1,0)</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Reward</b></li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: The Descendian Order (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Citizens of Underdocks (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Thieves_Guild_Bounty_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-thieves-guild-bounty-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-04</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-arson\"><summary><b>The Small Problem of Deepcut Arsonists</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl ?</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> 1 silver plus faction. Arsonists are an uncommon spawn in the Deepcut mining cave, and their oil is an uncommon drop.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Guard Darek</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>not listed</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive Small Storage Box from Guard Darek.; You receive 1 silver from Guard Darek.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Small Storage Box from Guard Darek.</li><li>Kill a Deepcut arsonist to collect 6 Vial of Flammable Oil. Arsonists are an uncommon spawn in the Deepcut mining cave, and the oils are an uncommon drop from them.</li><li>Combine the 6 oils within the box to craft Box of Oils.</li><li>Turn in the box to Guard Darek.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive 1 silver from Guard Darek.</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Small_Problem_of_Deepcut_Arsonists\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-the-small-problem-of-deepcut-arsonists\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-07</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Surface alternative: Shaded Dunes smugglers and wererats beach party (6-9, Toma the Two-Faced) and the Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane entrance (group 4-14), both through Night Harbor. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monme.no/camps\">monme.no camps (Petrichor&#x27;s database)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional, House Varros faction: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-underdocks-syrsil\"><summary><b>Syrsil&#x27;s Stolen Package</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl ?</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> XP and House Varros faction (a Deep Elf house). Senior Apprentice Syrsil is in the Inn tavern.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Senior Apprentice Syrsil</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Underdocks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>not listed</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>You gain experience!</li><li>Your faction standing with House Varros got better.</li><li>Senior Apprentice Syrsil says, &quot;Varsa ai Neth&#x27;xan! The Shadow must have sent you to me. Perhaps I am destined for greatness after all.&quot;</li><li>Senior Apprentice Syrsil says, &quot;May you hear.&quot;</li><li>Senior Apprentice Syrsil nods at you appreciatively.</li><li>*</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Syrsil%27s_Stolen_Package\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-syrsils-stolen-package\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-14</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Simrut the Green (after Marshal Harding)): L6 Net Shot; L7 Flare, Snaring Shot; L8 Interrupting Shot, Strafing Barrage I; L9 Piercing Shot I; L10 Alarm Trap, Point Blank II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Crescindy (sells Bard songs)): L6 Chant of Purity; L7 Repel; L8 Lento&#x27;s Aria of Stillness, Vellicosa&#x27;s Fanfare; L9 Languid Lullaby; L10 Dissonant Vocalization. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Gunder Dinnig (after Marshal Harding)): L6 Pounce; L7 Chop I; L8 Remedy Companion, Savage Spirit; L9 Command: Kill; L10 Enraging Strike II, Maul I. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Sister Marwen (trainer); Soren Akedd starts the quest): L8 Dispel Magic, Fear the Dead, Heal, Invisibility versus Undead, Lesser Redemption, Poison Protection, Promise of Mending I, Rebuke III, Resilience, Sense Magic, Shackle, Summon Food. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Luskmit): L8 Cure Disease, Mantle of Summer, Mantle of Winter, Prickly Barrier, Sense Magic, Speed of the Wild, Summer&#x27;s Warmth, Summon Drink, Summon Food, Swarm of Mites, Twisting Roots, Winter&#x27;s Chill. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L8 Companion Strike II, Dispel Magic, Flame Shield, Minor Creation: Fire, Summon Arrows, Summon Minor Manastone, Summon Minor Water Trident, Summon Throwing Dagger. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L8 Enchant Tin Bar, Illusion: Ogre, Lesser Enlightenment, Lesser Group Enlightenment, Lesser Vespyra&#x27;s Veil, Magic Protection, Minor Strength, Root, Runeskin, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Gunder Dinnig (after Marshal Harding)): L6 Armor Break; L7 Distracting Taunt; L8 Clobber, Intimidation; L9 Challenging Arrow I; L10 Rend II, Shield Bash I. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Silence, Ward of Suspicion; L7 Fire Protection; L8 Censuring Strike II, Dominate the Mind, Pillage Mana, Sense Magic; L9 Dispel Magic; L10 Purifying Blow, Scintillating Shock. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Sneak; L7 Pinning Throw; L9 Stone Stance; L10 Round Kick II. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Soren Akedd (starter quest)): L8 Aspect of Vampirism, Blood Pact, Dispel Magic, Eye of the Underworld, Feign Death (Spell), Holy Protection, Invisibility, Lesser Unliving Shield, Life Drain II, Pact of Deathly Enduring, Poisonous Deluge, Rot Flesh, Summon Minor Lifestone, Terrify the Dead. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Invisibility versus Undead; L7 Shield Toss; L8 Crusader Strike II, Fear the Dead, Healing Touch, Lay on Hands; L9 Blind; L10 Cure Poison, Restorative Smite. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Simrut the Green (after Marshal Harding)): L6 Swift Shot; L7 Invisibility versus Beasts; L8 Minor Mantle of the Hunter, Shroud, Taunt; L9 Barbed Shot, Twisting Roots; L10 Hunter&#x27;s Focus, Rending Cut, Survivor Stance. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Slylara Llumare): L6 Slice I; L7 Uppercut; L8 Sap; L9 Poison Tolerance; L10 Stab II. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Father Fyod (after Soren Akedd)): L6 Grip of Shadow; L7 Cold Protection, Holy Protection; L8 Grip of Agony, Shadow Strike II, Siphoning Slash, Soul Servant, Soulrend II; L10 Aura of the Unholy, Lord of Shadows, Pulling Shadows, Reave, Terror in the Shadows. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Picci Manifold): L8 Ancestor&#x27;s Eye, Ghostly Blight, Greater Malady, Invisibility versus Undead, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Pact of Haste, Pact of Renewal, Purge, Speed of the Wild, Spirit Bane III, Spirit Mending, Summon Food. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L6 Magic Protection; L7 Phase Strike; L8 Conduit, Dispel Magic; L9 Electricity Protection; L10 Discharge, Electric Infusion, Infused Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L8 Blink, Dispel Magic, Glyph: Mun, Insidious Magic, Lesser Spellshield, Minor Arcane Surge, Minor Iceblast, Sorcerous Mind, Spell Catalyst, Summon Mage Light. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul><p class=\"sc-nhnote\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The class notes below were written for a <b>Night Harbor</b> start (Night Harbor gates, the Night Market forge, Night Harbor camps). You picked Underdocks: use the route above for where to go.</p></div></div>";